    "title": "Michael Jackson’s Sons Prince & Bigi Support Their Cousin Jaafar Jackson at ‘Michael’ Movie World Premiere in Berlin!",
    "text": "Michael Jackson‘s family flew to Europe for the global fan premiere of the new biopic Michael! The late entertainer’s sons Prince, 29, and Bigi, 24, walked the red carpet at the event on Friday (April 10) at Uber Eats Music Hall in Berlin, Germany. The brothers were there to support the story of their father, as well as to support the performance of their cousin Jaafar Jackson, who portrays the iconic singer. Jaafar is the son of Michael‘s brother Jermaine Jackson. He was joined at the event by brothers Marlon and Jackie. Other cast members in attendance included Nia Long, Miles Teller, KeiLyn Durrel Jones, and Juliano Valdi. Notably absent from the event was Michael‘s daughter Paris Jackson, who has publicly criticized the movie. She called out the movie amid claims that she was “helpful” in production. The movie is set to be released in theaters on April 24. Watch a recently released clip! Here’s the synopsis: Michael is the cinematic portrayal of the life and legacy of one of the most influential artists the world has ever known. The film tells the story of Michael Jackson’s life beyond the music, tracing his journey from the discovery of his extraordinary talent as the lead of the Jackson Five, to the visionary artist whose creative ambition fueled a relentless pursuit to become the biggest entertainer in the world. Highlighting both his life off-stage and some of the most iconic performances from his early solo career, the film gives audiences a front-row seat to Michael Jackson as never before. This is where his story begins. Photos: Getty Posted to: Bigi Jackson, Celebrity Babies, Jaafar Jackson, Jackie Jackson, Jermaine Jackson, Juliano Valdi, KeiLyn Durrel Jones, Marlon Jackson, Michael, Michael Jackson, Miles Teller, Nia Long, Prince Jackson",
